course: dictionary
lesson: 6544
title: Newcomers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A newcomer is a person who has just arrived in a place, joined a group, or started something for the first time. «Teaching a newcomer is kinder than turning them away.» Here the newcomer is someone new to the class or school, and the sentence tells you that helping them is the kind choice.
explain: The word can be used in many places. In sport, you might read «a newcomer to the team». In a story about a new country, a newcomer might be a family who have just moved there and may be learning a new language. The clues around the word always tell you what kind of newcomer is meant.
explain: Look at the feeling in the sentence too. «Newcomers are busy and tired; the friendly thing is to say hello first instead of deciding they are «stuck up».» The sentence tells you what to do: say hello first, and do not judge a newcomer as unfriendly just because they are quiet.
fact: Newcomer is a noun. Its plural is newcomers.
fact: «Newcomer» means a person who has just arrived, joined a group, or started something for the first time.
fact: Newcomers can be new pupils in a class, new players in a team, or families who have just moved to a country.
fact: «Newcomers» in a school might need a friend to show them around and include them in games.
fact: «Stuck up» means thinking you are better than other people, so do not decide a newcomer is stuck up before you have said hello.
exercise: «Newcomers are busy and tired; the friendly thing is to say hello first.» What is a newcomer? | A dog that barks at strangers | A teacher who gives out homework | A person who has lived in the same house for years | *A person who has just arrived in a place or joined a group
exercise: «He is a newcomer to the team.» What does newcomer mean here? | A coach who picks the team | A player who has been in the team for ten years | A player who has just joined the team | *A player who is new to the team
exercise: Which word is the plural of newcomer? | newcomering | newcomes | newcomer's | *newcomers
test: «A dog or cat can feel jealous or scared when a new baby or a new pet arrives, so newcomers are introduced slowly, with an adult watching.» Why are newcomers introduced slowly? | Because newcomers are always late | *Because a pet or baby can feel jealous or scared when something new arrives | Because slow things are always better | Because an adult wants to go home early
test: «Teaching a newcomer is kinder than turning them away.» Which is the kinder choice? | Turn them away | Ignore them at break time | Tell them they are stuck up | *Teach them and help them settle in
exam: What is the friendly thing to do when a newcomer joins your class? | Wait for the teacher to do it | Ignore them until they speak first | Decide they are «stuck up» | *Say hello first and show them around
